<title>BELGIUM: EU says vets Westinghouse/Spain's SEPI deal.</title>
<headline>EU says vets Westinghouse/Spain's SEPI deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Monday it was starting a preliminary probe into a joint venture between Westinghouse Electric Corporation and Equipos Nucleares SA, a subsidiary of Spanish state holding SEPI.</p>
<p>The operation concerns the services supplied to operating nuclear and fossil-fuelled fuel plants that produce eletricity, the Commission said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said the deal was notified for clearance on November 21 under the European Union's merger rules. It has one month from that date to clear it or start a full, four-month probe.</p>
<p>Under the terms of the operation, Westinghouse and Equipos Nucleares will jointly control Westinghouse Technology Services SA and Enwesa Operaciones SA in the newly created venture.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom 322 2876841</p>
</text>
